      ":question/problem": "![](images/d0/d09a23a1ae9f737c7f19ba83d6d20c3fbcea3c7deb71fa307264c90afabc6580.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y+{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\u2216D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D\u2216R\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R\u2216D \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061y+{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y+{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$"
